\section{Principles}{
\itemize{
\item \strong{An anomaly is not misconduct.} Every row carries an \code{evidence_level}
from the shared metascience vocabulary: \code{signal}, \code{pattern},
\code{documentary} or \code{established}. Computations produce \code{signal}, or
\code{pattern} when independent signals converge; nothing computed is ever
\code{documentary} or \code{established}. Those levels require documents or
findings of an independent body, added by a person in a case.
\item Every signal lists its \strong{alternative explanations}.
\item \strong{No rankings of people.} Results are ordered by unit identifier, never by
score, and person-level signals need \code{include_individuals = TRUE}.
\item Corpus baselines are only as good as the corpus: differences across
fields, languages, regions and database coverage are a limitation of every
signal.
}
